-- ownership: calls (`ownership-checker.md` §6.1, and since slice 2 §16.4).
-- Slice 1 had no summaries and made a call's result a fresh list plus every
-- argument list its type could hold; slice 2 reads the same verdicts off
-- the callees' inferred summaries. `List.filter xs p : List Int` returns
-- `xs` itself when it keeps everything — the identity promise of thesis
-- §3.8, `res fresh, π1` — so extending it while `xs` is read later is
-- rejected, `call`, as the full checker does (T52's shape).
-- `List.map xs String.fromInt : List String` cannot be `xs`, a `List Int`
-- (§16.4's type filter on an identity promise): the extension is accepted,
-- `call`. `List.length` returns an `Int`, which crosses and holds nothing.
-- `[ …xs, …List.reverse xs ]` reads a temporary that may be `xs` while
-- writing `xs`: Disjoint fails only through the call's identity promise, so
-- it is rejected as `call` (thesis §8.4: an approximate tag).
pub filtered : List Int → Int
filtered xs =
    kept = List.filter xs λx → x > 0
    grown = [ …kept, 0 ]
    List.length grown + List.length xs


pub mapped : List Int → Int
mapped xs =
    labels = List.map xs String.fromInt
    grown = [ …labels, "end" ]
    List.length grown + List.length xs


pub counted : List Int → List Int
counted xs =
    n = List.length xs
    [ …xs, n ]


pub mirrored : List Int → List Int
mirrored xs = [ …xs, …List.reverse xs ]
